---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import PrivacyBadge from '../../components/PrivacyBadge.astro';
import JsonLd from '../../components/JsonLd.astro';
---
<BaseLayout title="Split PDF Locally — Extract Pages Without Upload | ZeroSend" description="Extract specific PDF pages or ranges into a new PDF directly in your browser. No source-file upload is required for processing.">
  <JsonLd data={{ '@context':'https://schema.org','@type':'WebApplication', name:'ZeroSend Split PDF', applicationCategory:'UtilitiesApplication', isAccessibleForFree:true }} />
  <section class="tool-page"><div class="container narrow-wide"><p class="eyebrow">PDF TOOL</p><h1>Split PDF</h1><p class="lead">Choose pages or ranges and create a new PDF locally.</p><PrivacyBadge />
    <div class="tool-shell" data-split><label class="dropzone"><strong>Choose one PDF</strong><span>We will read its page count in your browser</span><input type="file" accept="application/pdf,.pdf" /></label><div class="controls hidden" data-controls><p class="mini-note">Document: <strong data-name></strong> · <strong data-total></strong> pages</p><label>Pages to extract<input data-ranges type="text" inputmode="text" placeholder="1-3, 5, 8-10" aria-describedby="range-help tool-status" /></label><small id="range-help">Use page numbers and ranges separated by commas.</small><button class="button primary" data-process type="button">Extract pages</button></div><p class="status" data-status id="tool-status" role="status" aria-live="polite" aria-atomic="true"></p><div class="result hidden" data-result><div class="stats"><div><span>Selected pages</span><strong data-count></strong></div><div><span>Result size</span><strong data-size></strong></div></div><a class="button primary" data-download download>Download extracted PDF</a></div></div>
    <article class="content-block"><h2>How to split or extract PDF pages locally</h2><ol><li>Select one PDF.</li><li>Enter pages such as <code>1-3, 5, 8-10</code>.</li><li>Extract the selected pages.</li><li>Download one new PDF containing them in the requested order.</li></ol><h2>Why this v0.1 creates one output</h2><p>For the first version, “split” means extracting one or more ranges into one new PDF. A later version can add separate output files per range and package them into a ZIP locally.</p><h2>Limitations</h2><p>Encrypted PDFs, corrupted documents, and files that exceed available browser memory may fail. Files are limited to 50 MiB each, 100 MiB combined, and 2000 output pages. Files are limited to 50 MiB and 2000 extracted pages. Descending ranges and repeated pages are supported; empty comma entries are invalid. Complex PDF features are not guaranteed to transfer perfectly.</p><h2>FAQ</h2><h3>Can I repeat a page?</h3><p>Yes. If you specify the same page more than once, it can appear more than once in the output.</p><h3>Do you upload the PDF to discover its page count?</h3><p>No. The PDF library reads the selected file in your browser.</p><h2>Related tools</h2><p><a href="/tools/merge-pdf">Combine documents with Merge PDF</a></p></article>
  </div></section>
</BaseLayout>
<script>
  import { initSplitTool } from '../../scripts/pdf-tool';
  const root = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-split]');
  if (root) initSplitTool(root);
</script>
